commit e900207b9710f8e1b801e9ebbb022a697d87e40b

C03: uninstalling a plain name absent from the Start catalog is answered by its absence (INSTALL1631)

«Desinstala Worms Rumble» names no platform and nothing the Start catalog holds; the product removes nothing, and nothing can be removed that is not present. An uninstall of a plain one-to-four-word name outside the catalog now reads app.installed with the name as written — generic objects («todo», «esa app», «todos los juegos») stay with the model — and the composer says the name is not in the Windows Start catalog.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


